  "source": "Financial Sector Regulation Act 9 of 2017, s57 (Objective of the Financial Sector Conduct Authority). Authority: D-FSCA-REGULATORY-INTELLIGENCE-INGESTION.",
  "comment": "Regulatory-intelligence objective/mandate layer — FSCA. Mirrors the SARB-PA pilot (sarb-pa-objective-graph.json). The objective nodes (the 'why' a conduct requirement exists) are Plane-A reference data, re-derivable from the regulator's own statement of objectives (FSR Act 9 of 2017 s57), NOT events (D-REGULATORY-ARCHITECTURE-TWO-PLANE). PURSUES/SERVES/ALIGNS_TO edges target EXISTING graph nodes: Regulator REG-FSCA (seed-projection.ts Step 1); Obligation nodes OBL-ORG-* (Step 6, keyed OBL-<ORG-id>, from Regulations/_obligations.seed.json); Policy nodes POL-<policy-id> (Step 9, from Policies/*.md frontmatter policy-id). The FSR Act 9 of 2017 Document stub node DOC-FINANCIAL-SECTOR-REGULATION-ACT-9-2017 is also seeded by the SARB-PA objective artefact (importObjectiveArtefacts is idempotent — INSERT OR REPLACE), so this artefact only carries the ISSUED_BY edge to REG-FSCA (the same FSR Act establishes both authorities; PA per s33, FSCA per s57). SERVES wiring rationale: FSCA s57 names four sub-objectives. Fair-customer-treatment (TCF) is served by the FAIS / General-Code conduct obligations (ORG-CD-*, ORG-FAIS-*, ORG-FAIS-RK-*) and the OTC-derivative-provider conduct-toward-counterparty obligations (ORG-ODP-COND-*, ORG-CS2-001). Market-integrity (efficient & fair markets, market-abuse) is served by the FMA market-abuse / market-conduct obligations (ORG-MK-01..05, ORG-FMA-*), the ODP authorisation obligations that keep the OTC market orderly (ORG-CS1-*, ORG-ODP-AUTH-*), and the trade-reporting obligations that deliver market transparency (ORG-CS3-*, ORG-ODP-RPT-*, ORG-MK-RPT-*). financial-inclusion and financial-education are FSCA statutory objectives with no bank-adopted obligation that currently serves them in the build phase — the objective nodes are recorded (PURSUES + REFINES) but carry no SERVES edge yet, mirroring the PA pilot's treatment of objectives nothing yet serves. ALIGNS_TO wiring: the conduct-bundle policies align to fair-treatment; the markets-bundle policies align to market-integrity. Residual ALIGNS_TO gaps (recorded 2026-06-10, WS-REG-INTELLIGENCE-OBJECTIVE-LAYER tail-fill): financial-inclusion and financial-education carry NO aligned policy by deliberate decision, not omission — both are FSCA-directed statutory functions under FSR Act s.57(a) (the FSCA provides education programmes and promotes inclusion), and the build-phase bank has no retail customers or products (customer lifecycle activates at licence-day), so no existing policy genuinely serves either objective; a fabricated edge would be worse than the visible gap. They surface as advisory findings in recon:objective-policy-alignment until a consumer-facing policy estate exists. The mandate-level objective carries no direct ALIGNS_TO by design — mandate coverage is transitive via the REFINES roll-up in recon:objective-policy-alignment. Every SERVES/ALIGNS_TO target id was confirmed present in the seeded graph (OBL-ORG-* from the seed; POL-* from Policies/*.md frontmatter).",
